import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 311 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Institutional-Alternative Benefit: Injecting Anchor Symbiosis into Shrouding-the-Heavens World","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 311 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Institutional-Alternative Benefit: Injecting Anchor Symbiosis into Shrouding-the-Heavens World","no":311,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Institutional Alternative Benefit","Anchor Symbiosis","Quantitative Benefit","Civilizational Reform"],"related":["22-Resource Distribution by Joint Contracting Mechanism","25-Symbiotic Feedback Loop Mechanism","29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0311_模块2-遮天-制度替代收益.md","filePath":"en/0311_模块2-遮天-制度替代收益.md"}'),a={name:"en/0311_模块2-遮天-制度替代收益.md"};function s(r,e,l,u,h,d){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-311-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-institutional-alternative-benefit-injecting-anchor-symbiosis-into-shrouding-the-heavens-world" tabindex="-1">Entry 311 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Institutional-Alternative Benefit: Injecting Anchor Symbiosis into Shrouding-the-Heavens World <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-311-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-institutional-alternative-benefit-injecting-anchor-symbiosis-into-shrouding-the-heavens-world" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 311 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Institutional-Alternative Benefit: Injecting Anchor Symbiosis into Shrouding-the-Heavens World&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 24) | Benchmark base: Documents 22, 25, 29</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-what-happens-when-heng-yuan-zhou-s-institutions-are-put-into-shrouding-the-heavens-world" tabindex="-1">Introduction: What happens when Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s institutions are put into Shrouding-the-Heavens world <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-what-happens-when-heng-yuan-zhou-s-institutions-are-put-into-shrouding-the-heavens-world" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: What happens when Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s institutions are put into Shrouding-the-Heavens world&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the collective ascension axiom requires institutions to feed back to Myriad Ranks; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires governance power to belong to Myriad Ranks. This entry quantifies the benefit of &quot;injecting Anchor Symbiosis institutions into Shrouding-the-Heavens world,&quot; contrasting with Entry 310&#39;s &quot;Ye Fan-absent collapse simulation.&quot; The law-first axiom requires: benefit must be quantifiable, not stay at &quot;it would be better.&quot; Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Wastes eliminated after institutional injection:</p><ul><li>Emperor lifespan idle-runs → strong-one post-duty system, lifespan must be used for civilization feedback</li><li>Knowledge buried with the dead → Alaya real-time recording, lifelong Dao insights searchable whole-network</li><li>Resource zero-sum contention → joint contracting, more work more gain, develop increment Origin</li><li>Single-generation genius bet → 20% Activation Strategy broadly cultivates the backbone</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After institutional injection regression is rooted out:</p><ol><li>Dark-turmoil cycle → Alaya early warning + life-circulation system public, harvesting-lives-to-extend path cut off</li><li>Person present = policy flourishes, person dead = policy dies → order constitutionalized, tied to no one</li><li>Knowledge generational break → cultivation knowledge perpetually online, later-generations-restart cycle terminated</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After institutional injection, Ye Fan&#39;s predatory structure is gradually dismantled:</p><ul><li>Physique privilege → Myriad-Ranks differentiated paths public</li><li>Opportunity zero-sum → increment development enlarges the cake</li><li>Dao legacies hidden → 300 systems fully public</li></ul><p>Ye Fan may still be a strong one, but he no longer enjoys three privileges: &quot;resource priority, knowledge monopoly, rule exemption.&quot;</p><p>Institutional-alternative benefit can also be viewed from &quot;time compound interest.&quot; Ye Fan alone suppressing: benefit positive during Ye Fan&#39;s in-office period, but immediately turns negative once he leaves, and deeply negative. After institutional injection, early construction cost is higher, but benefit compounds over time — after a millennium, institutional benefit far exceeds Ye Fan-alone suppression&#39;s peak. This is the essential difference between solitary Dao and institutions: solitary-Dao benefit is pulsed, present only when the person is present; institutional benefit is compound, thicker the longer it lasts. What Myriad Ranks want is not a lifetime pulse, but ten thousand years of compound interest.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This entry&#39;s core — quantitative benefit table:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Pre-Reform</th><th>After Symbiotic Institutions</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dark turmoil millennium outbreak count</td><td>5–8</td><td>0</td><td>−100%</td></tr><tr><td>Myriad-Rank governance participation rate</td><td>&lt;5%</td><td>&gt;60%</td><td>+12×</td></tr><tr><td>Mid-low strong-one success rate</td><td>Baseline</td><td>Several times</td><td>↑ several times</td></tr><tr><td>Knowledge-transmission rate</td><td>30%</td><td>95%+</td><td>↑3×</td></tr><tr><td>Post-Ye-Fan civilization survival rate</td><td>30%</td><td>99%+</td><td>↑3×</td></tr><tr><td>Civilization-energy millennium curve</td><td>Oscillation</td><td>Continuous rise</td><td>Qualitative change</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate pre-reform Shrouding-the-Heavens world</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: simultaneously inject Alaya supervision + 300-systems public + Myriad Ranks republicanism + joint contracting</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: six metrics above</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: conclusion — institutional-alternative benefit comprehensively crushes &quot;relying on Ye Fan alone suppressing,&quot; and benefit amplifies over time</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Post-reform setting self-consistency</strong>: high</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk</strong>: zero</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: drops from medium to extremely low — Ye Fan from &quot;civilization pillar&quot; to &quot;one of first-generation anchors&quot;</li></ul><p>Institutional-alternative benefit should also subtract &quot;reform cost.&quot; Any institutional transition has labor pains: old oligarchs may resist, Myriad Ranks may not adapt to new rules. But Quest Sediment Domain simulation shows the pain period is about one or two epochs, after which benefit rises exponentially. The cost of maintaining the old system is ongoing — the dark-turmoil price paid every epoch. Comparing the two on a ten-thousand-year scale, institutional-alternative benefit ratio reaches tens to one. Ye Fan alone suppressing continuously pays old-system cost; institutional alternative pays transition cost once, then long-term benefit.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: eliminate four wastes — idle-run, burial, zero-sum, genius-bet</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: dismantle three predations — physique privilege, opportunity zero-sum, Dao legacies hidden</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s academy prototype is only a single-point reform; this plan is full institutional injection</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Myriad Ranks from &lt;5% participation to &gt;60%, a qualitative change</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: reformed Shrouding can serve as a cross-multiverse civilization template</li></ul><p>Institutional-alternative benefit should also include a &quot;soft power&quot; dimension: a civilization with institutions is more easily trusted and joined by other star regions. Ye Fan&#39;s oligarchic civilization cannot export order outward, because other star regions worry &quot;after I join, do I also have to listen to the Ye family?&quot; Republicanized civilization, because institutions are transparent, instead becomes an attraction center for cross-star-region cooperation.</p><ul><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Institutional-alternative benefit is not &quot;about the same,&quot; but an order-of-magnitude gap. Ye Fan alone can protect one lifetime of peace; one set of institutions can protect ten thousand generations of Myriad Ranks — this is solitary Dao vs. symbiosis&#39;s settlement.</p><p>Institutional-alternative benefit calculation should also subtract &quot;cultural transition cost&quot; — Myriad Ranks from &quot;wait for Ye Fan to arrange&quot; to &quot;arrange themselves&quot; requires generations to learn self-governance. But Quest Sediment Domain simulation shows this cost is far below the cost of maintaining dark turmoil. Short-term labor pain for long-term peace is civilization history&#39;s most cost-effective trade.</p><p>Ultimately, institutional alternative is not a negation of Ye Fan, but responsibility to Myriad Ranks. Ye Fan has done well enough; Myriad Ranks deserve a future that does not depend on Ye Fan. This is the ultimate lesson Heng Yuan Zhou extracts from the Shrouding-the-Heavens system.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · institutional-alternative benefit described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./310_模块2-遮天-求索域复盘.html">Entry 310 · Quest Sediment Domain Review</a> · <a href="./308_模块2-遮天-锚点共生替代方案.html">Entry 308 · Anchor Symbiosis Alternative</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">22-Resource Distribution by Joint Contracting Mechanism</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',35)])])}const g=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
